          "Land of Nairi (Երկիր Նաիրի, Yerkir Nairi) is a novel in three parts by Yeghishe Charents, written between 1921 and 1925 and published as a book at Yerevan in 1926. Charents did not call it simply a novel: he described it as a պոեմանման վեպ, a poem-like novel, and the label is not decoration. Long passages of lyrical and essayistic prose interrupt the narrative, the narrator addresses the reader directly, and the story of a city's collapse is told less as a sequence of events than as a mood the reader is made to sit inside.",
